   "rawMarkdown": "I'm wondering if a simple detector -> crop pipeline could help here, especially for subtle meniscus/ligament findings.\n\nSomething along the lines of:\n\n```python\nbbox = detector(image)\nroi = crop(image, bbox, margin=0.15)\nprediction = model(roi)\n```\n\nHas anyone tried this? Curious whether the extra localization step gives a meaningful gain over using the full FOV, or whether things like edema/effusion are better handled with the full image.\n",
   "content": "<p>I'm wondering if a simple detector -&gt; crop pipeline could help here, especially for subtle meniscus/ligament findings.</p>\n<p>Something along the lines of:</p>\n<pre><code>bbox = detector(image)\nroi = crop(image, bbox, margin=0.15)\nprediction = model(roi)\n</code></pre>\n<p>Has anyone tried this? Curious whether the extra localization step gives a meaningful gain over using the full FOV, or whether things like edema/effusion are better handled with the full image.</p>",
